("premiere",None,"La Traviata premiered on 6 March 1853 at La Fenice in Venice.","It was first performed on 6 March 1853 at La Fenice opera house in Venice."),
("composer",None,"The day after the premiere, Verdi wrote his most famous letter: \u201cLa traviata last night a failure. Was the fault mine or the singers\u2019? Time will tell.\u201d","La traviata last night a failure. Was the fault mine or the singers'? Time will tell.","Performance_history","Verdi, letter to Emanuele Muzio, 1853 (via Wikipedia)"),
("premiere",None,"The premiere audience jeered at times, some of it aimed at the casting of Fanny Salvini-Donatelli as Violetta.","The audience jeered at times during the premiere, directing some of their scorn at the casting of soprano Fanny Salvini-Donatelli","Performance_history"),
("history",None,"Revised and revived in 1854, it was a hit. Piave reported: \u201cThen it was a fiasco; now it has created a furore. Draw your own conclusions!\u201d",["it was a fiasco; now it has created a furore. Draw your own conclusions!"],"Performance_history","Francesco Maria Piave (via Wikipedia)"),
("history",None,"Verdi wanted a contemporary setting, but La Fenice insisted on the past (\u201cc. 1700\u201d). Realistic modern-dress productions came only in the 1880s.",["the authorities at La Fenice insisted that it be set in the past, \"c. 1700\"","It was not until the 1880s"]),
("history",None,"The story comes from La Dame aux cam\u00e9lias by Alexandre Dumas fils, which Verdi saw in Paris with Giuseppina Strepponi in 1852.",["It is based on La Dame aux camélias (1852), a play by Alexandre Dumas fils","In February the couple attended a performance of Alexander Dumas fils'  The Lady of the Camellias."]),
("trivia_" if False else "history",None,"By coincidence, an Italian translation of the Dumas play was running just down the street from La Fenice at the premiere.","an Italian translation of the play La Dame aux camélias was being presented just a short distance from La Fenice","Performance_history"),
("composer",None,"Verdi told Piave he wanted something new: \u201cI don\u2019t want any of those everyday subjects that one can find by the hundreds.\u201d","I don't want any of those everyday subjects that one can find by the hundreds.","Composing_for_Venice","Verdi to Piave (via Wikipedia)"),
("composer",None,"Verdi arrived in Venice for rehearsals \u201cfilled with premonitions of disaster\u201d and made his unhappiness clear to the singers.","Verdi was filled with premonitions of disaster upon his arrival in Venice on 21 February for rehearsals","Composing_for_Venice"),
("music","Prelud|Preludio","The prelude opens with very soft, very high strings portraying the frail heroine, then the main love theme on lower strings.","The prelude to the opera begins with very soft, very high strings depicting the frail heroine","Music"),
("music","Libiamo","Asked for a toast, Alfredo sings the brindisi \u201cLibiamo ne\u2019 lieti calici\u201d, \u201cLet\u2019s drink from the joyful cups\u201d.","Libiamo ne' lieti calici","Act_1"),
("music","Libiamo|Che \u00e8 ci\u00f2|Un d\u00ec, felice","After the Brindisi, an offstage band plays waltzes. Waltz rhythms run through Act I to create a Parisian atmosphere.","waltz rhythms pervade the first act of the opera, creating a Parisian atmosphere","Music"),
("music","Pura siccome|Dite alla giovine|Madamigella Valery","The long Germont\u2013Violetta duet is built in many sections, the music following each turn of the drama.","is multi-sectioned with the music following the changing dramatic situation","Music"),
